  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "timer_inventory",
      "result": "THREE_STOCK_START_CALLS_MAP_TO_TWO_TIMERS; BOTH ARE CANCELLED TWICE",
      "details": "Stock Ghidra maps vibrator state+0x330 to vibrator_init/vibrator_work_routine and audio state+0x520 to haptic_init/haptic_audio_store/audio_timer_func. Current candidate disassembly confirms the two init offsets, the three start callsites, shutdown checks in callbacks/work wrappers, and aw_remove cancels both timers before and after draining their work. LED-child unregister drains the haptic_audio_store producer before timer teardown."
    },
    {
      "id": "probe_misc_registration",
      "result": "NO_PARTIAL_MISC_REGISTRATION_LEAK_PATH_FOUND",
      "details": "Current candidate aw_i2c_probe calls the stock-exact body under the lifecycle transition mutex. In the current ELF, haptic_lifetime_misc_register is called immediately before g_aw_haptic is published, with no recoverable branch between; the helper records the registration result. Probe-completion gating rejects opens during setup. On later probe setup failures the wrapper routes cleanup through aw_remove, whose current block path deregisters only a successfully registered and published misc device."
    },
    {
      "id": "ram_firmware_callback_lifetime",
      "result": "CALLBACKS_DRAINED_BEFORE_STATE_RETIREMENT; MODULE_REFERENCE_PINNED_BY_TARGET_LOADER",
      "details": "Current candidate increments the outstanding callback count before request_firmware_nowait, passes __this_module, and rolls the count back on synchronous failure/shutdown. The callback serializes, releases firmware after shutdown or calls ram_load while active, then decrements/wakes the count. aw_remove cancels delayed work, drains callbacks, cancels delayed work again, then destroys the workqueue and retires state. The pinned firmware loader invokes the callback before put_device/module_put and guards release_firmware against NULL."
    }
  ],
